<title>SPAIN: Spain to set 2.6 percent minimum wage rise.</title>
<headline>Spain to set 2.6 percent minimum wage rise.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's minimum wage increase in 1997 will be 2.6 percent, in line with forecast inflation, Secretary General for Employment Manuel Pimentel said on Monday.</p>
<p>Speaking at a news conference after a meeting with businessmen and trade union groups, Pimentel added that the increase would be approved at the next cabinet meeting.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
